				</ukm:Metadata><Secondary><Body DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/nisi/1996/1320/body" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/nisi/1996/1320/body" NumberOfProvisions="132" RestrictExtent="N.I." RestrictStartDate="2022-10-26"><Part DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/nisi/1996/1320/part/II" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/nisi/1996/1320/part/II" NumberOfProvisions="24" id="part-II" RestrictStartDate="2022-10-17"><Number>PART II</Number><Title>TRIAL</Title><Pblock DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/nisi/1996/1320/part/II/crossheading/trial" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/nisi/1996/1320/part/II/crossheading/trial" NumberOfProvisions="16" id="part-II-crossheading-trial" RestrictStartDate="2014-10-31"><Title><Emphasis>Trial</Emphasis></Title><P1group RestrictStartDate="2006-01-01"><Title>Mode of trial</Title><P1 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/nisi/1996/1320/article/13" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/nisi/1996/1320/article/13" id="article-13"><Pnumber>13</Pnumber><P1para><Text>An offence against a provision of the Road Traffic Orders specified in column 1 of Part I of Schedule 1 or against regulations made under such a provision (the general nature of which offence is indicated in column 2) shall be punishable as shown against the offence in column 3 (that is, on summary conviction or on indictment or in either one way or the other).</Text></P1para></P1></P1group></Pblock></Part></Body></Secondary></Legislation>